{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You grew weary from your many journeys.</b> From the many ways you repeated, and you grew weary — yet you did not say, 'My heart despairs,' as in ונואש ממנו שאול (1 Samuel 27:1). Rather you said, perhaps my toil will avail:" "<b>The life of.</b> Like כח (strength), and the meaning joins with יגעת (you grew weary): therefore you did not grow weak."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:56.958431829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}